INTERPRETATION
All polynomial arithmetic uses boost::rational<cpp_int>.  The stable
calculation exhausts the seven activation intervals of the ordinary
sixth- and seventh-power multiplicities.  Q=1,2 are checked directly;
the remaining regions have nonnegative monomial coefficients after the
displayed exact cone substitutions and boundary-strip refinements.

At K=2Q+1 the Kac--Walton formula has the first reflected image pair and,
for the seventh power near the upper endpoint, one further negative image.
Q=1,...,10 are checked directly.  For Q>=11 the listed fixed-width and
two-slack regions exhaust 0<=Y<=2Q+1, and every pulled-back margin has
nonnegative rational coefficients.  An independent finite-fusion
recurrence checks 15,000 sixth- and seventh-power formula coordinates
through Q=40 in the nearest and stable bands.

The result proves only K=2Q+1 and K>=7Q.  The intermediate affine band
2Q+2<=K<7Q remains outside this certificate.

